000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, MAY 6, 2009\r\rMayor Wolfson called the meeting to order at 7:33 p.m. in the City Council Chambers, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Wolfson, Mayor pro Tem Groveman, Councilmembers Bozajian, Washburn and Maurer.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Ballin, Bingham, Coroalles, Rice, Starns, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\r The Pledge of Allegiance was led by Dr. Donald Zimring, Superintendent, Las Virgenes Unified School District.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r \r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\r The City Council presented a proclamation to Taryn Wayne, Historic Preservation Commission Chairperson for Historic Preservation Month.\r\rA presentation was given by Debbie Bruschaber, Mountains Restoration Trust, regarding �A Bridge Across Time, Connecting People with Wildlands,� Headwaters Corner at Calabasas Master Plan, 2008.\r\rThe Las Virgenes Unified School District and students gave a presentation on an anti-apathy program for teens based on the book �7 Habits of Highly Effective Teens� by Steven Covey.\r\rCouncilmember Bozajian announced that the Calabasas Historical Society�s Annual Old Town Western Barbeque will take place on Sunday, June 14 at the Leonis Adobe. He also thanked the Arts Council and City staff for a successful Arts Festival which took place last weekend, in particular Laureen Morick for her usual fine effort. In addition, Councilmember Bozajian thanked staff and volunteers who participated in the annual Las Virgenes Creek Cleanup event. Councilmember Maurer announced that an electronic waster roundup will be held on Saturday, May 9 at Albertsons on Agoura Road, from 10:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. Councilmember Washburn mentioned that a rose specialist will be speaking at the Leonis Adobe on Saturday, May 9 from 2:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m. and encouraged all to vote on May 19. Mayor Wolfson reminded everyone about the Relay for Life event being held on Saturday & Sunday, May 15 & 16 at A.E. Wright Middle School.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r No indicated a desire to speak.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of Professional Services Agreement with James Dean for Landscape Architecture and City Arborist Services in the amount of $50,000.00. \r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2009-258, approving the pre-zoning of the Mont Calabasas Annexation Area (Permit No. PL08000613) in conformance with the land-use policies of the Calabasas General 2030 General Plan and in preparation for submission of an application to the Los Angeles County Local Area Formation Commission seeking annexation of the Mont Calabasas area to the City of Calabasas. \r\r Approval of the extension of the Venco Western, Inc. contract completion date for one year from May 3, 2009 to May 3, 2010 for Specification No. 05-0602 Landscape Maintenance of the common areas within individual Homeowner Associations and common benefit areas within Landscape Maintenance District No. 22 and Landscape Lighting Act District No. 22.\r\r Recommendation to award a construction contract for Project Specification No. 08-09-04 to Silvia Construction Inc., and award $135,000 to Pavement Engineers, Inc. for Consulting Services.\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve the Consent Items. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rSPECIAL ITEM\r\r5. Consideration of Letter of Support for Senate Bill 696, (Wright) � AQMD Emission Reduction Credits.\r\r Leeor Alpern, Senior Public Information Specialist, South Coast Air Quality Management District gave a presentation on Senate Bill 696 and urged support.\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to continue this item to the May 20, 2009 City Council meeting. MOTION CARRIED 4/0 (Mayor pro Tem Groveman absent from dais). \r \rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r6. Recommendation from the Historic Preservation Commission to approve file No. 090000071 and adopt Resolution No. 2009-1184 designating the William C. Masson House, located at 23075 Mulholland Highway, as a Local Historic Landmark.\r\r Mayor Wolfson opened the public hearing.\r\r Debbie Bruschaber spoke in support of the item.\r\r Mayor Wolfson closed the public hearing.\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to adopt Resolution No. 2009-1184. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r\r7. Introduction of Ordinance No. 2009-256, repealing Chapter 12.04 and adding Chapter 8.34 relating to graffiti abatement.\r\r Building Official Sparky Cohen presented the staff report.\r\r Councilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to introduce Ordinance No. 2009-256, amended to add language in Section 8.34.040 regarding unresponsive owner or agent. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r8. Approval of appointments by Mayor pro Tem Groveman to the Communications and Technology Commission, Environmental Commission, Historic Preservation Commission, Library Commission, Park, Recreation and Education Commission, Planning Commission, Public Safety Commission, and Traffic and Transportation Commission. \r \r Councilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to re-appoint Linda Massarella (Groveman) to the Communications and Technology Commission for terms expiring March 2011. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Councilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to re-appoint Stuart Cohen (Groveman) to the Environmental Commission for terms expiring March 2011. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Councilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to re-appoint Jason Peirce (Groveman), to the Historic Preservation Commission for terms expiring March 2011. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Councilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to re-appoint Mark Shear (Groveman) to the Parks, Recreation and Education Commission for terms expiring March 2011. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Councilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to re-appoint David Brown (Groveman) to the Planning Commission for terms expiring March 2011. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Councilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to re-appoint Diana Brenke (Groveman) to the Public Safety Commission for terms expiring March 2011. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Councilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to re-appoint Robert Friedman (Groveman) to the Traffic and Transportation Commission for terms expiring March 2011. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r9. Check Register for the period of March 5, 2009 to April 9, 2009. \r\r There was no action taken.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles stated that he met with School District officials and would report on that meeting to the City Council at the budget meeting. He also reported on the meeting with the Rubicon Theatre Group.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r Councilmember Bozajian requested that staff review the possibility of the Library extending hours during finals week. Councilmember Maurer requested an update on compliance with the City�s ordinance on second hand smoking in apartments be scheduled on the August 12 City Council agenda.\r\r\u000b\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ADJOURN \r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:03 p.m. to the next regularly scheduled meeting on Wednesday, May 20, 2009 at 7:30 p.m.\r\r\r\r\r__________________________________________________\rRobin Parker, Acting City Clerk\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\r05/06/09\r\u